# text = I believe that in a certain Eastern Empire it was not uncommon for a man who wished to provide for his family to offer himself as a substitute for a criminal condemned to execution on the understanding — an undertaking which I believe was always honourably observed — that adequate recompense should be paid to his dependants after his demise .
