# text_id = 1731
# text = Under the conditions which obtain in the lowland area , the old doctrine of benefit dons not seem to be a -sufficient test for the fair incidence of charge , and it appears to be just to supplement that contribution by one representing the cost to the lowlands of the necessary engineering work for avoiding the water from those upland areas .
