# text_id = 1797
# text = I find that in 1918 no less than 422,805 people passed through the National History Museum , and in 1919 that figure had increased to the substantial number of 455,736 , illustrating the point that quite obviously there is a very deep and increasing interest on the part of the general public in the exhibits at the National History Museum .
