# text_id = 1826
# text = The people who before the War were accustomed to pay tax are confronted with the alternative of abandoning their average pre-War savings or greatly reducing their standard of living , and in nearly every case , as is evident from the ordinary evidence of everyday life , they have chosen to abandon their savings rather than reduce their standard of living .
