# text_id = 1855
# text = The second and third - class mines of to - day were the first - class mines of the past ; but the industry was not organised as it should have been , or it would have kept a portion of the huge profits gained when coal was near the bottom of the shaft to meet the growing expenses as the coal face got further and further away from the shaft .
