# text_id = 1864
# text = On that main point I made it clear to the Council that the liberty of the British representative was safeguarded with regard to this particular appointment , and that whatever might be the view about other appointments this country reserved its liberty to treat this appointment , against which it protested , and for which I refused to vote , as standing on rather an exceptional and peculiar basis .
