# text_id = 1868
# text = I have been through a good many telephone exchanges , and I realise that the operator must look at the lamp , and plug the right hole , and how that can be managed before you actually take the receiver from the machine and put it to your ear , is to me a marvel and a mystery , and I think the Post Office is entitled to credit for it .
