# text_id = 1871
# text = It is difficult to give figures for 1920 comparable with those for later years , owing to alterations of frontiers ; but the excess of imports over exports , and re-exports , of merchandise in our trade with Soviet Russia , as declared for the three years 1921 – 23 was , roughly , £ 7,500,000 , and for the two years 1924 – 25 , roughly , £ 14,500,000 .
