# text_id = 1889
# text = A considerable sum of money is expended on these civilian instructors , but I venture to say in regard to the moral effect a cadet is likely to learn a great deal more from an instructor who has on him the glamour of his doings during the late War than from a man , however learned and distinguished , who has spent most of his time in some university town .
