# text_id = 1906
# text = If we go to the industrial districts or Lancashire we , find that in Ashton , a cotton town , in Bury , a cotton town , and in Accrington , a cotton town , there was not a single case of milk adulteration in 1925 or 1926 , and taking the bulk of the towns there it will be found that the adulteration figure is below 10 per cent .
