# text_id = 1912
# text = Experience of that Act has shown that defectives have frequently been unable to receive the treatment which they ought to receive and from getting the help which they ought to have , for there is no doubt that , when available , the care and training provided under the 1913 Act have proved of the greatest help to defectives and given them a great deal of happiness and assistance .
