# text_id = 1914
# text = It was quite true that the exchange value of the pound sterling rose while the party opposite were in power , and they claimed that as being to their credit , but the hon . Member would not be conscious that that meant a nearer approach to the gold standard because in those days he had not decided what he believed in and was not studying these things very carefully .
