# text_id = 1922
# text = Brigadier - General CLIFTON BROWN ( by Private Notice ) asked the Chancellor of the Exchequer whether , in view of the numerous allegations that the Government have failed adequately to carry out the recommendations of the Lytton Committee on the subject of the extended employment of ex-service men in the Civil Service , he will be willing to appoint a special Committee of Inquiry to look into the matter ?
