# text = In the second place , it makes special provision for a class of houses peculiar to Scotland — the houses of the small landowners or crofters who , owing to their remote situation and the difficulties they have in obtaining material and in finding sufficient time to devote to the construction of their houses , have not hitherto been able to benefit by the provision of the State subsidy .
