# text = The Air Minister is subject , there is no doubt , to be attacked suddenly , and particularly by the naval interest , and it is the duty of this House and those who believe in unity and the value of a unified Air Service to make that point of view quite clear and to answer the arguments , especially of the soldiers and the sailors on that point .
