# text = Lieut .- Colonel Sir FREDERICK HALL asked the Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs whether the arrangements made by him from time to time for interviews with representatives of the Allied Governments for the preliminary discussion of matters of common interest follow the practice in this respect which was established between 1918 and 1922 when the Prime Minister of the day was acting as de facto head of the Foreign Office ?
