# text_id = 1943
# text = Even if the drains do not overflow their banks the sub - soil is of such a porous nature that the additional pressure of water in the drains will cause the adjoining land to become so flooded or water - logged as to destroy or damage the valuable crops grown thereon and render the land unfit for cultivation and it would eventually revert to its former state of swamp .
