# text_id = 1954
# text = Local authorities already have powers under the Housing ( Additional Powers ) Act , 1919 , for prohibiting building operations which interfere with the erection of houses , and I am of opinion that further powers are necessary , as the present powers in many districts have been found to be insufficient to limit quite unessential buildings which further increase the difficulties arising from the shortage of skilled building labour .
