# text = As a matter of fact , Clause 13 of this Bill is worse than the Poor Law Act of 1927 , because under that the recovery of relief by way of loan is given as a power and not as a duty , and Section 47 of that Act gives the power to recover from a friendly society annuity or periodical payment , while Section 13 here gives no such power .
