# text_id = 2005
# text = If they expect the country to believe that there is any merit in the claim that the British unemployed man is to be put in touch with the soil , might I remind them that we are importing £ 700,000,000 worth of foodstuffs , and a proportion of it could be grown in this country if they had the courage to tackle this vital problem of a land - locked nation .
